  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADB Core Environment Programme (CEP)                  Phase II, 2012-2017 - ADB CEP II GMS 2012-2016</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ADB Core Environment Programme (CEP)                  Phase II, 2012-2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Core Env Program (CEP) omfattar fyra omr&#xe5;den: (i)                     milj&#xf6;planeringssystem, metoder och f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade skydds&#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder, (ii)   hantering av gr&#xe4;ns&#xf6;verskridande omr&#xe5;den f&#xf6;r biologisk m&#xe5;ngfald och    f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttring av lokala f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjningsm&#xf6;jligheter, (iii) klimatresilienta investeringar och strategier f&#xf6;r minskade koldioxidutsl&#xe4;pp samt (iv)  st&#xe4;rkande av institutioner och milj&#xf6;f&#xf6;rvalning.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Core Env Program (CEP) comprises four outputs: (i) environmental  planning systems, methods and safeguards improved; (ii) management of trans-boundary biodiversity conservation landscapes and local         livelihoods improved; (iii) climate resilient investments and low     carbon strategies developed; and (iv) institutions and financing for  sustainable environmental management strengthened.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme&apos;s main outcome objective is an &quot;Environment-friendly and climate-resilient GMS Economic Cooperation Program&quot;. The CEP goals were to (i) create an environmentally friendly and ecologically rich GMS to enhance the environmental sustainability of the GMS Economic Cooperation Program and (ii) improve biodiversity conservation and climate resilience across the GMS.</narrative>
  </description>
